Next, nitro precursor undergoes SNAr (template 1914397) to introduce bromine? Actually template 1914397 is for SNAr where amine attacks aryl bromide? The mapped_rxn product side is target (with amine). The precursors from apply_template-3: ["CC(C)(C)OC(=O)N1CCNCC1", "O=[N+]([O-])c1cc(Br)c2c(c1)CCC1(CCC1)O2"] So that splits into a simpler amine core (no aromatic) and a nitro-bromo aromatic fragment. So reaction node template_id 1914397 with two children: core amine (mol) and aromatic nitro-bromo (mol).

Next, the aromatic nitro-bromo fragment undergoes bromination (template 1914398) to add bromine? Actually template 1914398 is electrophilic bromination forward, so retrosynthetic step removes bromine to give precursor without bromine. The apply_template-4 gave precursors: ["BrBr", "O=[N+]([O-])c1ccc2c(c1)CCC1(CCC1)O2"] So reaction node template_id 1914398 with children: "BrBr" (bromine source) and the aromatic nitro (no bromine) fragment.

